{"id": "EUVD-2026-86948", "enisaUuid": "842b25f5-9544-3c2c-bb6a-50d81b79fe8c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncachefiles: Fix potential UAF/KASAN warning\n\nCurrently, trace_cachefiles_coherency() is being passed a pointer to a\n__be64 lain over the coherency data in struct cachefiles_xattr so that it\ncan display the first 8 bytes.  However, the data is of variable length and\ncould even be 0 bytes.  This could lead to a UAF or KASAN warning.\n\nFix this by making sure the buffer has room for at least 8 bytes and that\nthose 8 bytes are pre-cleared.\n\nFurther, those bytes are not 8-byte aligned, so fix the tracepoint to\nextract the data as four 2-byte words (they are 2-byte aligned) and\nreassemble the __be64.  The compiler will convert this into a single 8-byte\nload where the CPU supports it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68d459e6e609c31f96a203dd6eec60c634f155e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93488ea378b4427598cace558236c110515d743b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a67632c8c2688d6e0091529bcefe54bc5ee80e9b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98117", "GHSA-57px-gx57-6w68"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c8e2a93-a443-3845-a597-466114243fb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "229105e5cfd9832a9ef1368c96e0098ec3a5fbf0 <93488ea378b4427598cace558236c110515d743b"}, {"id": "37adef03-0638-33ef-8004-2ac50bd602ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "540476ac-a50a-38d0-8707-8a55c2f99077", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7cea752e-dbce-3446-b24a-d419464e9049", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "a780103e-42a1-301f-a74e-558142d89194", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "d2127b5f-7125-3438-953d-4503682f42bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d660c776-4da2-39ed-a603-3e55828e2b7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "229105e5cfd9832a9ef1368c96e0098ec3a5fbf0 <68d459e6e609c31f96a203dd6eec60c634f155e1"}, {"id": "fa714594-ebe3-36ee-8ce2-2e2f85b827e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "229105e5cfd9832a9ef1368c96e0098ec3a5fbf0 <a67632c8c2688d6e0091529bcefe54bc5ee80e9b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "49fcc3a8-e6db-34ae-8709-cc1e9c153c15", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}